# Hardware arrival + assembly

@hw_bundle OpenBCI All-in-One Biosensing R&D Bundle (Cyton + Daisy + Dongle + Mark IV helmet + 2 ear clips + 1 Y-splitter + 500mAh Li-Po + USB charger)
@hw_arrival 2026-04-28 (mid-session — boards + helmet + battery on-site, user assembling)
@hw_battery_charged confirmed (charger LED green)
@hw_y_splitter_count 1 (NOT 2 — standard OpenBCI single-splitter config)

@y_splitter_decision SRB2 reference path only. BIAS handled directly via second ear clip → Cyton BIAS socket. Daisy SRB2/BIAS shared via Cyton+Daisy stack header pins (automatic). Rationale: SRB2 is THE critical reference signal; with single Y-splitter, allocate to highest-priority path. BIAS less sensitive to ground-loop than SRB2.

@user_wiring_self_report
  - ear clip 1 → Cyton hardware-row position 1 (= BIAS) directly, BLACK wire
  - ear clip 2 → Y-splitter male pin (Y-splitter SRB2 path)
  - Y-splitter socket A → Cyton hardware-row position 3 (= SRB2)
  - Y-splitter socket B → unused (insulated)
  - 16 EEG color wires → Cyton/Daisy bottom row N1P-N8P (per OpenBCI Mark IV doc table)

@stack_recovery_event tick T+8min: user reported all Daisy ch 11-16 RAILED in OpenBCI GUI; subsequent tick "Data from the board doesn't change" verdict on ch 9-16. Diagnosis: Daisy stack pin loose. Recovery: power cycle Cyton OFF→PC + Daisy reseat → 16/16 ADC alive on next read.

# Software stack patches (5 hexa files, 16 file edits, all uchg-locked post-edit)

@patch_argv_parser_aot_safe 5 files patched (anima-eeg/calibrate.hexa, eeg_recorder.hexa, experiment.hexa + new board_health_check.hexa + new electrode_adjustment_helper.hexa). Reason: hexa argv() returns binary path duplicated under AOT mode + interpreter-wrapper variant /Users/ghost/.hx/packages/hexa/build/hexa_interp.real. Original `_flags_only_argv()` only matched .hexa suffix in argv[0], leaked exe path as first "flag". Patch: skip leading args ending in .hexa OR .real OR /exe OR starting with /. ALSO uses .ends_with() method form (raw#9 AOT-safe — slice equality fails under AOT codegen).

@patch_brainflow_version_attr 2 files patched (calibrate.hexa, eeg_recorder.hexa). Reason: brainflow 5.21.0 doesn't expose __version__ attribute. Patch: replace `import brainflow; print(brainflow.__version__)` with `from importlib.metadata import version; print(version('brainflow'))`.

