# hexa-lang gaps surfaced (raw#159 upstream-proposal-mandate)

@gap_1_streaming_subprocess BLOCKER for true real-time tools. hexa exec(cmd) blocks + buffers stdout. No `popen_lines()` or Process.stdout.read_line() API. Workaround: helper Python self-renders, hexa wrapper just invokes. Proposed API: `for line in popen_lines(cmd) { ... }`. Cost ~150-300 LoC self/stdlib/process.hexa.

@gap_2_map_has_method map type lacks .has() / .contains_key() method. Workaround: string-based _kv_lookup(body, key). Proposed: stdlib map.has(key) / map.get(key, default) / map.keys(). Cost ~50 LoC.

@gap_3_ansi_escape_string_literal `"\x1b[2J"` produces literal chars `\x1b[2J` not ESC byte 0x1B. Workaround: os.system('clear') in helper Python. Proposed: lexer recognize \x1b, \033, \uXXXX in string literals. Cost ~20-50 LoC self/lexer.hexa.

@gap_4_argv_normalization_redundancy 8+ tools across hive/anima/nexus duplicate _flags_only_argv() (8 distinct copies observed). stdlib/flags.hexa exists but most tools don't `use` it. Proposal: migrate to stdlib + audit. Cost ~30 LoC stdlib audit.

@gap_5_string_slice_eq_aot s[(n-5)..n] == ".hexa" works in interpreter but fails in AOT-compiled binary. Workaround: .ends_with() method form. Proposed: AOT codegen for slice equality should preserve interpreter semantics. Cost ~50 LoC self/codegen_c2.hexa.

@upstream_dispatch_status nexus kick run "hexa-lang-upstream-popen-lines-map-has-ansi-escape-from-anima-eeg-live-mode-blocker" dispatched to hetzner 2026-04-28T16:30 (90s timeout reached, witness landing async). raw#100 strengthening clause: kick-FAIL fallback authorized but kick still in-flight. Will check witness landing later.

# raw#10 honest C3 disclosures

@raw10_c3_disclosure_1 Touch detection on no-helmet floating wires = empirical heuristic (rms deviation + mains pickup change). Not validated against ground-truth touched-vs-not-touched dataset. Tuning is iterative. Real validation requires helmet-on + actual EEG signal baseline.

@raw10_c3_disclosure_2 BOARD_PINS_SHORTED verdict in no-helmet state is documented FALSE-POSITIVE. Cross-channel correlation > 0.95 is normal when all floating wires share environmental EMI. Real pin shorts can only be confirmed in helmet-on condition.

@raw10_c3_disclosure_3 Y-splitter SRB2-only allocation (vs ideal 2-splitter SRB2+BIAS) is a compromise driven by single-splitter inventory. Daisy BIAS sharing via stack pins is reliable IF stack is firm; observed once-per-session loose-stack failure mode (recovered via power cycle).

@raw10_c3_disclosure_4 ANSI escape compatibility: ghostty + macOS Terminal.app verified by user. tmux + VSCode terminal NOT tested. Fallback os.system('clear') added but tput backend may differ across terminals.

